NDI: chain version=1.0

-----------------------------------------------------
This file was created from the file 'radlib_ndi_v2.0'
by removing the v2.0 features not in the v1.0 format.
-----------------------------------------------------

Full documentation for this file may be found in reference:

Morgan C White. "Release of NDI Formatted Libraries 'radlib', 'y21grp' and 'y21grp_n',"
Los Alamos National Laboratory memorandum X-5:MCW-03-13 (January 22, 2003).

This file contains the yttrium (Y), thulium (Tm), iridium (Ir) and lutetium (Lu)
chains that are commonly known as the 'radlib' chain library.  The original version
of radlib did not include lutetium.  When the original chain information was updated
to include lutetium, several other updates occured as well.  All changes are noted by
appropriate comment sections in the chain table.  (1) The yttrium chain was resequenced
to remove unused reactions; these included the serveral inelastic reactions that were
given but had products that were considered to have decayed immediately back to the
ground state and an (n,3n) reaction that contained all zero values as it did not
threshold in until after the top energy in the 21 group structure.  (2) The thulium
chain was extended to include generic destruction reactions for some targets.  This has
been further extended herein to include destruction reactions for all targets.  (3) The
iridium chain was resequenced to remove one unused inelastic reaction.  This file attempts
to be the superset of the two previous radlib chains and prefers the original number
sequences where available.  The additional reactions added during the update are simply
added as continuing sequence numbers past the last original number.  Obviously, lutetium
uses the sequence numbers from the updated radlib file.

All chains on this file have library_name equal 'radlib'.

The chains specified within this file are appropriate for use with dosimetry data from
the libraries:

  Chains            Dosimetry Data Library Names

   y.001zrc         y21grp or y21grp_n
  tm.001zrc         y21grp or y21grp_n
  ir.001zrc         y21grp or y21grp_n
  lu.001zrc                   y21grp_n (ONLY)

\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/\|/
The use of these chains with dosimetry data other than above may give erroneous results.
/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\/|\



